+# M9-07 implementation and evaluation handoff
+
+**Status: BLOCKED.** Task M9-07; date 2026-10-06; direct requirement ROB-07, related AI-04/PAN-01 and ROB-02–ROB-06; acceptance AC-10/AC-11 **not complete**. No checklist or shared progress file was edited by this worker.
+
+## Revision and scope
+
+Tested baseline/review base: `441ce9be5b914aa12ed918629663195f32e97d03`, branch `ftc-workspace`. This documentation checkpoint retains product baseline `d7aca195c0a47fadb0fc3788eefbe96f99ec68be`. The focused task commit is identified in the coordinator handoff; the tested delta consists only of:
+
+- `docs/validation/robot-action-isolation.md` and this report.
+- `docs/validation/m9-07/` raw output.
+- `packages/core/test/ftc-evaluation/m9-07.test.ts`.
+- `packages/core/test/ftc-adapters/action-boundary-probe.test.ts`.
+- `packages/core/test/ftc-adapters/fixtures/action-boundary/process.ts`.
+- `packages/desktop/src/main/panels-policy.ts`.
+
+No changes to existing command/build routes, module wiring, public APIs, generated clients, durable Session behavior or shared checklists. No real robot mutation occurred. No new dependency was introduced.
+
+The only production-source addition is an immutable **disabled evaluation decision**, with no consumer and no I/O. It is deliberately not advertised as enforced Electron isolation. The executable evaluation uses real child processes and owned loopback listeners, with fixture broker/controller messages and a generated local Gradle task. It does not instantiate M9's future production broker.
+
